<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.4.4: Solving Equations Using the Zero Product Property and Reasoning</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02148</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.4.4: Solving Equations Using the Zero Product Property and Reasoning</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2992e87a-af6e-4448-aa05-b6f5b41db7ff</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">Find all solutions to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. Explain or show your reasoning.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Enter the solutions to the equation and your reasoning.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00004"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00005">By the zero product property, either <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, so <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
